Article 12
(1) The Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children has the duties to: a. promote the Protection of Women and Children to the community on an ongoing basis;
b. carry out socialization and advocacy of the Protection of Women and Children to government officials and the community;
c. formulate a regional action plan for the Protection of Women and Children; d. prepare an annual work program;
e. encourage the realization of planning and budgeting that supports the Protection of Women and children; and
f. formulate recommendations for regent policies.
(2) The Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) is responsible to the Regent.
